# Agent notes (self-evolve)

`docs/NOTES.md` is the live unresolved scratchpad (caps in
`scripts/check-hot-docs.mjs` — do not count lines by hand).
Measured objectives/scores live in **`docs/CURRENT.md`**, fixed causes in
`DIVERGENCE-LOG.md` (+ `DIVERGENCE-INDEX.md`), structural omissions in one
`docs/c-js-map/*.md` section, and loop chronology in the journal **tail**
(archive older entries under `docs/archive/`).

## What belongs in NOTES.md

- Active hypothesis + one command that would falsify it
- Current expensive dead ends labeled “don’t re-check” (cap ~15)
- Session landmarks still needed live (cap ~15)
- Open questions only — not peel chronology or resolved causes
- When suite is PASS: remind map-driven / cluster density (not FAIL peels)

## What does not

Constitution, strategy essays, resolved peel chronology, baseline scores,
completed D-chains, and module status — those have other owners (`CURRENT.md`,
archive, divergence, c-js-map).

## When to write

After any diagnosis that burned a long wrong path, add 3–5 lines to
`docs/NOTES.md` **before** the next peel. Once resolved, move the evidence to
`DIVERGENCE-LOG.md` + index row and remove stale detail from Notes. Prefer
falsifying against **key/RNG maps** early; for geometry / flip / land **or**
keystream / `more` / `NEED_MORE`, prefer a **temp C dump at the cited locus**
over screens, JS `FORCE`, or another topline shim (playbook §7).

## Self-reflect

Update Notes when evidence shows the working theory is wrong. Ordinary loop
porters must not rewrite this rule, the Constitution, or the runbook; propose
process changes in the journal for human/auditor review. Drop the theory—do
not invent alignment machinery to save it.
